# Patch/merge backups. `patch` and `git` drop these next to the file they came
# from, so a `git add -A` while one exists commits a byte-for-byte duplicate of
# a source file under a name nothing imports — silent, and easy to miss in a
# large diff. Observed during the C4 review, when a prototype patch left
# src/pdf/layout.js.orig behind.
*.orig
*.rej

